 reading: nu_L > 1 exactly when m_L < n C_L (coefficient descent); mu_L + nu_L = 1 - log_3(eta_L)/L <= 1; the Ridout
  product sits at exponent exactly 2 with constant eta_L (n C_L)^2 >= 1 (Ridout needs 2 + eps and an algebraic target)
== (7) the Apery-form recurrence A_(L+1) = 3 A_L + 2^(v_2(A_L)) ==
 oddpart(A_L) = m_L and v_2(A_L) = d_L along every orbit of odd n < 2*10^5 (4041077 steps), and A_L = 3^L n C_L exactly for n < 2000: True
 so d_L = log_2(3^L n C_L) - log_2 m_L: the 2-adic exponent d_L/(L log_2 3) exceeds 1 by exactly log_2(n C_L/m_L)/(L log_2 3)
== (8) Borel-Dwork radii of F_w(z) = sum 2^(d_k) z^k: R_oo R_2 = 2^(liminf d_k/k - limsup d_k/k) <= 1 ==
 Sturmian valuation word d_k = ceil(k log_2 3): letters [1, 2], running means d_k/k at k = 10, 100, 1000, 10000: [1.6, 1.59, 1.585, 1.585] -> log_2 3 = 1.5850; R_oo = 1/3, R_2 = 3, product 1
 (1 2)^oo (cycle of -5): mean valuation 3/2 = 1.5000 < log_2 3 (in E_inf), R_oo = 2^(-1.5000), R_2 = 2^(1.5000), product 1; F_w rational (periodic exponents)
 (1 1 1 2 1 1 4)^oo (cycle of -17): mean valuation 11/7 = 1.5714 < log_2 3 (in E_inf), R_oo = 2^(-1.5714), R_2 = 2^(1.5714), product 1; F_w rational (periodic exponents)
 random 2-adic points (4000-bit odd seeds, 1500 steps): mean valuation d_k/k in [1.937, 2.060] (Terras: 2), all > log_2 3: coefficient descent, R_oo < 1/3
 verdict: every Collatz series has R_oo R_2 <= 1 -- the Borel-Dwork criterion (R_oo R_p > 1 forces rationality) is never applicable; the boundary is populated by irrational series (Sturmian words: Theorem S)
